   "record": "fc999c02e8f7ea0a1888a242ac927bd99aec4e43b28151df82031f2de07b6dcd",
   "status": "MISMATCH",
   "ruling": "Ruling: scope; refusal located elsewhere. i1040sca p. 8, Line 8a, 'subtract the amount shown on Form 8396, line 3, from the total deductible interest'. A mortgage credit certificate is asked by s3.mcc when mortgage interest is entered and refuses Schedule 3 line 7 and the return through s3.mcc_if_interest (Form 8396), so no computed return reaches line 8a with the credit (fixture redesign.credits.refuse.mcc). Same ruling as the earlier round; the line was re-reviewed because lane fx-itemized changed the mortgage interest help (a rented property's interest is left out).",
   "subject_key": "dd2a0684499486e291cdc8b5dab970f7f2a99806875d3aba69c6e18c257bfa08"
  },
  {
   "key": "11",
   "record": "fc999c02e8f7ea0a1888a242ac927bd99aec4e43b28151df82031f2de07b6dcd",
   "status": "MISMATCH",
   "ruling": "Ruling: finding; p526 p. 5, Exception, 'If the state or local tax credit you receive or expect to receive doesn't exceed 15% of your payment amount ... your charitable contribution deduction isn't reduced'. The line 11 source leaves out every credit-earning part. Already filed as BUG-1086 (open); the foreign-organization point is the source's own rule (i1040sca p. 10, gifts to foreign organizations), with the Canadian, Israeli and Mexican treaty charities a narrow residual within BUG-1086's review. Re-reviewed only as a reader of the changed lines.",
   "subject_key": "72255534603fa9cc7ccd3e2a1807fdfed528cbe4549a1d167d1f9164e939b732"
  },
  {
